<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SPFN Mobile — the Compose example app's manifest.

  It declares NO permissions, and INTERNET is the one it used to. There was a path here
  that built a client against a server local.properties named; nothing reached it, because
  this app has no enrolment path of its own and every call that client made was refused for
  want of a key. The menu replaced that path, on the same fake every cell runs on, so this
  app now cannot send whichever way it was launched — which is a stronger statement than
  the one the permission used to sit beside.

  Predictive back is DECLARED here, and it has to be. `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback`
  is what makes the system deliver a back gesture to the window's OnBackInvokedDispatcher
  instead of down the legacy KEYCODE_BACK path, and on Android 13 to 15 it is off by default
  whatever the target SDK — the target-SDK default only flips at Android 16. Undeclared,
  androidx's OnBackPressedDispatcher still receives the completed back and everything still
  navigates, so nothing looks broken; what never arrives is the PROGRESS, so
  `NavigationHost`'s `predictivePopTransitionSpec` has nothing to animate. On a Galaxy Z
  Flip4 running Android 15 the screen being popped sat still under the held gesture with only
  the system's arrow drawn over it, and the screen underneath appeared on release
  (docs/IMPLEMENTATION-PITFALLS.md P35).

  The theme is this app's OWN, over the system parent it used to name directly:
  res/values/themes.xml, one attribute, no new dependency. It was a bare
  Theme.DeviceDefault.Light.NoActionBar until a dark-mode Galaxy Z Flip4 drew the status
  bar's clock and icons in a light foreground over this app's white — barely legible on the
  menu and the sheets, invisible over a pushed screen. That is a property of the WINDOW, so
  the app declares it: `android:windowLightStatusBar`, which the resource file explains and
  which nothing in the SDK can or should reach.

  Everything the parent decided, it still decides. No action bar, because left unset an app
  inherits the platform's default and that draws a title bar of its own above the
  composition: on the 3e emulator round every Android screenshot carried an "SPFN Example"
  strip over the SDK's own header where iOS had one header and nothing else. `android:label`
  still names the app in the launcher and in the task switcher; what changed is that no
  window decoration draws it a second time. DeviceDefault and not Material or AppCompat,
  because this repository depends on no design system it did not write (decision C2) and
  either of those would be a new artifact in gradle/verification-metadata.xml for a window
  background. `Light` and not the appearance-following variant, because `SpfnTokens`
  resolves to the same white palette in both appearances: a theme that went dark on a
  dark-mode device would paint `FlowHost.cover()` — which reads `android:colorBackground`
  off the host's theme, and is the one attribute every Android theme defines — near-black
  behind screens that are still white.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <application
        android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"
        android:label="SPFN Example"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.SpfnExample">

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>

    </application>

</manifest>
